#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `nvidia-*-cu12` versions can change when the environment is rebuilt. Code that depends on an exact CUDA library version might need updates after a new release.\n"
msgstr "Puwedeng magbago ang mga bersyon ng `nvidia-*-cu12` kapag muling ginawa ang environment. Maaaring kailanganing i-update ang code na umaasa sa eksaktong bersyon ng CUDA library pagkatapos ng bagong release.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Request a package {#request-a-package}"
msgstr "Humiling ng package {#request-a-package}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If other users would also need a package, [request it on GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). An accepted package is added to the environment in a later release. Until then, or for a private package, [add it as a wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"
msgstr "Kung kailangan din ng ibang user ang isang package, [humiling sa GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). Idadagdag sa environment ang tinanggap na package sa susunod na release. Hanggang doon, o para sa private na package, [idagdag ito bilang wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: issue #2017 removes the request template, but the public PR Qiskit/qiskit-serverless#2651 keeps it. Confirm that the link remains. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add your own packages {#add-your-own-packages}"
msgstr "Idagdag ang sarili mong mga package {#add-your-own-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use a package that is not installed, collect its wheel files on your computer, upload them to the workflow's file storage, and install them at the start of the workflow. You upload them again only when they change.\n"
msgstr "Para gumamit ng package na hindi naka-install, kolektahin ang mga wheel file nito sa computer mo, i-upload ang mga ito sa file storage ng workflow, at i-install ang mga ito sa simula ng workflow. Uulitin mo lang ang pag-upload kapag nagbago ang mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build wheels {#build-wheels}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng mga wheel {#build-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The job installs wheels without an internet connection, so each wheel must work with Python 3.12 on Linux (x86_64). Collect the wheels in one folder:\n"
msgstr "Nag-i-install ang job ng mga wheel nang walang internet connection, kaya dapat gumana ang bawat wheel sa Python 3.12 sa Linux (x86_64). Kolektahin ang mga wheel sa iisang folder:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`Local terminal`**\n"
msgstr "**`Local terminal`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `--platform` and `--python-version`, `pip download` gets wheels for the job's platform, even when you run it on macOS or Windows. It also downloads the package's dependencies, such as `python-dateutil`, `six`, and `tzdata` for `pendulum`. Because the job installs each wheel without its dependencies, upload a wheel for every dependency that the environment lacks, and delete the other wheels from the folder.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang `--platform` at `--python-version`, kumukuha ang `pip download` ng mga wheel para sa platform ng job, kahit patakbuhin mo ito sa macOS o Windows. Dina-download din nito ang mga dependency ng package, gaya ng `python-dateutil`, `six`, at `tzdata` para sa `pendulum`. Dahil ini-install ng job ang bawat wheel nang walang mga dependency nito, mag-upload ng wheel para sa bawat dependency na wala sa environment, at burahin sa folder ang iba pang mga wheel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A pure-Python wheel (`py3-none-any.whl`) works on any platform. If a package with compiled code has no Linux x86_64 wheel on PyPI, build one on Linux, for example in a `python:3.12` container. Keep the original file names, because `pip` reads the package name, version, and platform from them.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana sa kahit anong platform ang pure-Python na wheel (`py3-none-any.whl`). Kung walang Linux x86_64 na wheel sa PyPI ang isang package na may compiled code, gumawa ng isa sa Linux, halimbawa sa isang `python:3.12` container. Panatilihin ang orihinal na mga pangalan ng file, dahil binabasa ng `pip` ang pangalan ng package, bersyon, at platform mula sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload wheels {#upload-wheels}"
msgstr "I-upload ang mga wheel {#upload-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the wheels from your local notebook with `add_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "I-upload ang mga wheel mula sa local notebook mo gamit ang `add_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each path can be a file name or a glob pattern, and `add_wheels()` returns the names of the uploaded wheels. If a pattern matches no files, or matches a file that is not a `.whl` file, `add_wheels()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat path ay puwedeng pangalan ng file o glob pattern, at ibinabalik ng `add_wheels()` ang mga pangalan ng na-upload na mga wheel. Kung walang file na tumutugma sa pattern, o may tumugmang file na hindi `.whl` file, nagtataas ang `add_wheels()` ng `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow before you add wheels, because the wheels are stored with it. They go to a `wheels` folder in the workflow's [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows), separate from your other files.\n"
msgstr "I-upload ang workflow bago ka magdagdag ng mga wheel, dahil iniimbak ang mga wheel kasama nito. Napupunta ang mga ito sa isang `wheels` folder sa [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) ng workflow, hiwalay sa iba mong mga file.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace or remove wheels {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"
msgstr "Palitan o alisin ang mga wheel {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see the wheels that are uploaded to a workflow, call `list_wheels()`. To remove wheels, pass their file names to `remove_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "Para makita ang mga wheel na na-upload sa isang workflow, tawagin ang `list_wheels()`. Para mag-alis ng mga wheel, ipasa ang mga pangalan ng file nito sa `remove_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade a package, remove the old wheel, and then add the new one. A new version has a different file name, so if you keep the old wheel, `install_uploaded_wheels()` installs both versions.\n"
msgstr "Para i-upgrade ang isang package, alisin ang lumang wheel, tapos idagdag ang bago. May ibang pangalan ng file ang bagong bersyon, kaya kung iiwan mo ang lumang wheel, ini-install ng `install_uploaded_wheels()` ang parehong bersyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install wheels in your workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"
msgstr "I-install ang mga wheel sa workflow mo {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit your workflow code to call `install_uploaded_wheels()` before it imports the packages:\n"
msgstr "I-edit ang code ng workflow mo para tawagin ang `install_uploaded_wheels()` bago nito i-import ang mga package:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`install_uploaded_wheels()` installs every wheel in the `wheels` folder. If the workflow has no wheels, the call does nothing. The wheels are installed again in every run, so a large set of wheels adds to the start time of each job.\n"
msgstr "Ini-install ng `install_uploaded_wheels()` ang bawat wheel sa `wheels` folder. Kung walang mga wheel ang workflow, walang ginagawa ang tawag. Muling ini-install ang mga wheel sa bawat run, kaya ang malaking set ng mga wheel ay nagdaragdag sa oras ng pagsisimula ng bawat job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: bring only missing packages {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"
msgstr "Best practice: dalhin lang ang mga package na kulang {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, upload wheels only for the packages that the environment lacks. A wheel for an installed package, such as `numpy`, installs a second copy, and the code that imports it can get either copy. Errors from a mismatch appear only when the job runs.\n"
msgstr "Bilang best practice, mag-upload lang ng mga wheel para sa mga package na kulang sa environment. Ang wheel para sa naka-install nang package, gaya ng `numpy`, ay nag-i-install ng pangalawang kopya, at puwedeng alinman sa dalawang kopya ang makuha ng code na nag-i-import nito. Lumalabas lang ang mga error mula sa hindi pagkakatugma kapag tumatakbo na ang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you upload, check your requirements with `dependency_report()` from your local notebook:\n"
msgstr "Bago ka mag-upload, suriin ang mga requirement mo gamit ang `dependency_report()` mula sa local notebook mo:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report gives each requirement one of the following statuses:\n"
msgstr "Binibigyan ng report ang bawat requirement ng isa sa mga sumusunod na status:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`baked`: The environment already provides the package. Do not upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`baked`: Ibinibigay na ng environment ang package. Huwag mag-upload ng wheel para dito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`bring`: The environment lacks the package. Upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`bring`: Kulang sa environment ang package. Mag-upload ng wheel para dito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`clash`: The environment provides a different version. Change the version that your code requires, or rebuild your package for the installed version.\n"
msgstr "`clash`: Ibang bersyon ang ibinibigay ng environment. Baguhin ang bersyong kailangan ng code mo, o muling buuin ang package mo para sa naka-install na bersyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report checks only the supported packages, so it shows `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, and `numpy` as `bring`. The environment includes them, so do not upload wheels for them. The report shows `clash` only for an exact `==` version. It shows a range, such as `>=0.10`, as `baked`. The report does not upload any files.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri lang ng report ang mga suportadong package, kaya ipinapakita nito ang `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, at `numpy` bilang `bring`. Kasama na ang mga ito sa environment, kaya huwag mag-upload ng mga wheel para sa kanila. Ipinapakita lang ng report ang `clash` para sa eksaktong bersyon na `==`. Ipinapakita nito bilang `baked` ang isang range, gaya ng `>=0.10`. Hindi nag-a-upload ng anumang file ang report.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot dependencies {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"
msgstr "I-troubleshoot ang mga dependency {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` fails inside the workflow. | The job cannot reach the internet. [Upload a wheel](#add-your-own-packages) instead. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a package that you uploaded. | The workflow imports the package before it calls `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a dependency of a package that you uploaded. | Wheels are installed without their dependencies. Upload a wheel for the missing dependency. |\n"
"| The error says that a wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | The wheel is for another operating system or Python version. Get a wheel for Python 3.12 on Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` fails with `ResolutionImpossible`. | The `wheels` folder has two versions of the same package. Remove the old wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| A CUDA package, such as `cupy`, fails on a GPU compute profile after you upload wheels. | A wheel replaced one of the [CUDA packages](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| An installed package, such as `numpy`, fails after you upload wheels. | A wheel installed a second copy of a package that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Sanhi |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `pip install` sa loob ng workflow. | Hindi maabot ng job ang internet. [Mag-upload na lang ng wheel](#add-your-own-packages). |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` para sa package na in-upload mo. | Ini-import ng workflow ang package bago nito tawagin ang `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` para sa dependency ng package na in-upload mo. | Ini-install ang mga wheel nang walang mga dependency nito. Mag-upload ng wheel para sa kulang na dependency. |\n"
"| Sinasabi ng error na ang isang wheel ay `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | Para sa ibang operating system o bersyon ng Python ang wheel. Kumuha ng wheel para sa Python 3.12 sa Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang `install_uploaded_wheels()` na may `ResolutionImpossible`. | May dalawang bersyon ng parehong package ang `wheels` folder. Alisin ang lumang wheel gamit ang [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang isang CUDA package, gaya ng `cupy`, sa GPU compute profile pagkatapos mong mag-upload ng mga wheel. | Pinalitan ng isang wheel ang isa sa mga [CUDA package](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) na ibinibigay ng environment. Alisin ang wheel na iyon gamit ang [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang naka-install na package, gaya ng `numpy`, pagkatapos mong mag-upload ng mga wheel. | Nag-install ang isang wheel ng pangalawang kopya ng package na ibinibigay ng environment. Alisin ang wheel na iyon gamit ang [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
